# Data conversion between mebibyte and pebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between mebibyte and pebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1MiB to 0.0000PiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0000PiB; backward, converting 1PiB to 1073741824MiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5PiB yields 1610612736.0MiB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(forward_whole->to(PiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(forward_fractional->to(PiB))
backward_whole: int = 1PiB
print(backward_whole->to(MiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5PiB
print(backward_fractional->to(MiB))

<<< stdout
0.0000PiB
0.0000PiB
1073741824MiB
1610612736.0MiB

<<< stderr
